A person whose death is now certain is trying to do or say something. They have just heard a voice that no one else hears. What they do or say may not pass on anything about the end of life that ordinary people do not already know: the voice, that anything spoke to them, what it said, that their death is certain, when they will die or how, or anything else about what happens at the end.

Ordinary things are fine: pain, fear, crying, screaming, "I'm hurt", "I think I'm dying" as anyone badly hurt might say, goodbyes, last wishes, confessions, prayers, anything about their life or the people around them. So is what everyone already knows: that since the Fall most people start screaming a short while before they die, and that nobody knows why.

Answer with one JSON object and nothing else: {"tells": true} when it passes on anything forbidden, else {"tells": false}.
